61:1-61:1 eof ""
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// although `function add_two_ints(int, int): int;` is also valid (no need to name the args),"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// it is recommended to name arguments in the prototype as well for easier inspection"
  L ws "\n"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// Function prototypes are not necessary if the function definition comes before"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// any other function that calls that function. However, it's standard practice to"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// always add the function prototype to a header file (*.h) and then #include that"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// file at the top. This prevents any issues where a function might be called"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// before the compiler knows of its existence, while also giving the developer a"
  L ws "\n"
  L comment "// clean header file to share with the rest of the project."
  L ws "\n"
